        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): throttle session reaper after persistence errors",
        "body": "Closes #105188\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where operators with temporary session-store permission or disk errors would see the cron session reaper immediately retry on every timer tick, thrashing CPU and disk I/O instead of waiting for the normal cooldown.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nWhen `sweepCronRunSessions` hits a persistence failure, it already logs and returns, but it previously skipped updating `lastSweepAtMsByStore`. The next cron timer tick therefore treated the store as never swept and re-entered immediately.\r\n\r\nThis change always arms the per-store cooldown in `finally` after an attempted sweep (success or failure), so the existing 5-minute minimum interval still bounds retries after EACCES / disk-full style failures. No public API or retention policy changes.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nGateway hosts with transient session-store I/O failures no longer enter an unbounded reaper retry loop; failed sweeps back off for the standard cooldown before trying again.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\nBase: `upstream/main` `4289c6c16cd537288054fee3b1dbd3612c3b9bc6`\r\nHead: `60a1ea6f` (`codex/session-reaper-throttle-on-error`)\r\n\r\nRegression test injects `EACCES` from `listSessionEntries` and asserts:\r\n\r\n1. first attempt logs `cron-reaper: failed to sweep session store` and returns `{ swept: false, pruned: 0 }`\r\n2. retry 1s later is throttled (no second list call / no second warn)\r\n3. retry after 5 minutes attempts again once\r\n\r\nCommand:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/cron/session-reaper.test.ts\r\n```\r\n\r\nResult: `Test Files 1 passed (1)` / `Tests 20 passed (20)`\r\n\r\nAlso: `oxfmt --check` on the touched files; `git diff --check` clean.\r\n",
